  "comment": "About 150 species of the southern California deserts: the 150 bird species with the most research-grade iNaturalist observations created up to 2026-09-27 across Imperial County (1528: the Salton Sea and the Imperial Valley), the Coachella Valley (51088: Palm Springs), Joshua Tree National Park (3680) and Anza-Borrego Desert State Park (118765), minus the domestic Muscovy Duck, plus desert birds heard more than seen (Common Poorwill, Lesser Nighthawk, Crissal and LeConte's Thrashers, Ridgway's and Virginia Rails; the rest of the hand list was already in; Western Screech Owl was dropped again: seven observations in the region gave one photo, and the bundled Los Angeles pack has its card). `packbuilder draft --place 1528 --place 51088 --place 3680 --place 118765 --before 2026-09-27 --top 150 --exclude 'Cairina moschata' --add ...`. scientific_name and common_name follow the BirdNET+ label file as in us-ca-la (species the committed packs already list reuse their entries); inat_taxon_id is iNaturalist's; wikipedia_url is iNaturalist's link for the taxon. The order is the observation ranking, then the species added by hand. Drafted with `packbuilder draft` (the command is below) and read over by a person; tests/test_definition.py checks the labels.",
